Data Type :

#1 - number

var a=5
console.log(a)
console.log(typeof a)

R : 5

#2 - string

var jc ='sprishya'
console.log(jc)
console.log(typeof jc)

R : sprishya

#3 - boolean

var jcvalid = true
console.log(jcvalid)
console.log(typeof jcvalid)
 R: True

******** Based on the value we assign data type will be considered.

#4 -  Undefined

var xyz
console.log(xyz)
console.log(typeof xyz)
R: Undefined

#5 - Null

var user = null
console.log(user)
console.log(typeof user)
R : null
R: OBJECT ** Null is originally a primitative data type . It pulls as OBJECT

****** Usage : user phone number , name field we do not know priorily , so we use null - in that box no values will appear or it will appear blank
in forms in web pages.
if suppose in that form - user leave as blank means - it will take the data type as undefined instead of null.

